*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store

# Claude Code.
#
# `.mcp.json` holds no credential TODAY — the Supabase server is an HTTP one and
# authenticates over OAuth, so the token lives in Claude Code's own storage, and
# `project_ref` is already public in the API URL that ships to every browser.
#
# It is ignored because of what the format allows next. A stdio MCP server is
# configured with an inline `env` block, so the natural way to add one is to
# paste an access token straight into this file — and `git add .` would then
# commit it silently and permanently. The upside of sharing it is one file a
# teammate can copy from .mcp.json.example; the downside is a write-scoped
# database token in the history forever. Not a close call.
#
# settings.local.json is per-developer by definition (it records which MCP
# servers YOU enabled). It happens to be covered by some global gitignores,
# which protects whoever set that up and nobody else on the team.
.mcp.json
.claude/settings.local.json
